Short:        VLC media player, unofficial OS3 port
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       VideoLAN (VLC); Amiga port: AmiCradle Team
Type:         gfx/show
Version:      0.1
Requires:     GFOpenRTG, GFOpenGPU, GFOpenMedia, AHI; GFOpenSocket for streams
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

An unofficial port of the VLC media player to AmigaOS 3.x, not made or
endorsed by VideoLAN.

A GadTools interface, with the drawing left to GFOpenRTG and GFOpenGPU: frames
stay in video RAM and are converted, scaled and composited by the graphics
board, subtitles and the on-screen display are alpha surfaces over the
picture, and full screen opens on any monitor. Decoding goes through GFOpenMedia
(the graphics chip's video engines, the GPU's on AmiCradle, a PiStorm's
VideoCore, or FFmpeg on the CPU), sound through AHI and network streams
through GFOpenSocket. Picasso96 and CyberGraphX systems get a slower fallback.

Status: planned; this readme is ready for the first release.

Licences: our Amiga modules are MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AmiCradle Team. VLC's
own code keeps its licences: libVLC, libvlccore and most modules are LGPL 2.1
or later, and the player and some modules GPL 2 or later. FFmpeg keeps its
own. The player as a whole is distributed under the GPL 2 or later, with every
licence text and the complete source in the archive. VLC and the cone are
trademarks of VideoLAN.

If you build on our part, we ask that you credit the AmiCradle Team and
AmiCradle.

Source: https://github.com/DalsinAI/gfopenvlc (the Amiga port) and
https://code.videolan.org/videolan/vlc (VLC)
